Q: How to change the DPI awareness setting of my .NET 4.8 WPF application? A: <p>I finally found the solution myself.<br />
The problem was that the MSIX project does not copy the manifest file from the output folder of my EXE project into the packaging output folder. Therefore all manifest settings are lost.</p>
<p>The solution is to <strong>embed the manifest into the MyApp.exe file</strong>, instead of having a MyApp.exe.manifest (which is a copy of app.manifest) file in the output folder. This can be achieved by editing the <strong>MyApp.csproj</strong> file.<br />
It contains this:</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>  &lt;PropertyGroup&gt;
    &lt;ApplicationManifest&gt;app.manifest&lt;/ApplicationManifest&gt;
  &lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>Just insert one extra line (with a text editor, because this option is not available in the VS 2026 project settings):</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>  &lt;PropertyGroup&gt;
    &lt;ApplicationManifest&gt;app.manifest&lt;/ApplicationManifest&gt;
    &lt;GenerateManifests&gt;false&lt;/GenerateManifests&gt;
  &lt;/PropertyGroup&gt;
</code></pre>
